1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,080
Listen to a talk in an anthropology class.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:08,057
Man: Often when we think of mummies,

3
00:00:08,057 --> 00:00:13,160
we think of ancient Egyptians and their elaborate methods of preserving bodies.

4
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:17,320
We used to think Egyptians were the only people

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,961
practicing mummification during the Bronze Age, about, oh,

6
00:00:21,961 --> 00:00:28,500
4000 years ago, because typical mummies are found in places, for example

7
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:31,280
with very dry climates like Egypt.

8
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:39,090
But then archaeologists discovered a site in Scotland with evidence of mummification.

9
00:00:39,090 --> 00:00:44,200
And Scotland is, well, wet, rainy.

10
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:49,980
This site is called Cladh Hallan, the only place in Britain

11
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:54,150
where we found prehistoric Bronze Age mummies.

12
00:00:54,150 --> 00:01:00,360
So researchers unearthed skeletons at Cladh Hallan, including a man

13
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:04,140
and a woman from around 1500 BCE.

14
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:07,080
Since these were just skeletons

15
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:12,180
the researchers didn't realize at first that they had actually been mummies.

16
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:20,000
That realization came after doing a test called radiocarbon dating on the bones.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,040
Radiocarbon dating revealed that the man

18
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:28,170
and woman had died several hundred years before being buried.

19
00:01:28,170 --> 00:01:33,927
Normally, such a long wait would turn a body into a pile of bones,

20
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:38,100
not an actual skeleton like what was found

21
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:45,160
So their bodies must have been purposely preserved for hundreds of years before burial.

22
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:49,070
Why? Well, who knows?

23
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:51,060
But we do know how.

24
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:57,050
The bodies were preserved, mummified in a peat bog.

25
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:00,760
Peat bogs are kind of like swamps,

26
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:03,900
except their conditions prevent organic materials

27
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:07,120
like bodies from fully breaking down.

28
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:10,000
They stay more intact.

29
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,826
Prehistoric people in Scotland used to preserve animal fat like butter in peat bogs,

30
00:02:17,826 --> 00:02:21,180
so they definitely had the concept.
